Great! Since everything is working now, let's walk through the architecture of your Hydro SCADA Dashboard and explain the purpose of each file and how data flows through the system.

Overall Architecture
MainWindow
    │
    ▼
MainDashboardViewModel
    │
    ▼
TrendCardViewModel (One per Tag)
    │
    ├── ScadaTag
    │
    ├── ChartSeriesViewModel
    │
    └── RenderableSeries
            │
            ▼
       SciChart Surface
1. ScadaTag.cs
Purpose

Represents a single SCADA signal/tag.

Example:

TANK_LEVEL
MOTOR_CURRENT
FLOW_RATE
PRESSURE

Contains:

Id
DisplayName
CurrentValue
Unit
MinValue
MaxValue
AxisTitle
ComponentType

Example:

Id = "LT101"
DisplayName = "Tank Level"
Unit = "%"
MinValue = 0
MaxValue = 100

Think of it as:

"Configuration + Current Value of a field device"

2. MainDashboardViewModel.cs
Purpose

Manages all trend cards visible on the dashboard.

Contains:

ObservableCollection<TrendCardViewModel>

Example:

Tank Level Card
Pump Pressure Card
Flow Meter Card

Stored in:

ActiveTags

When user adds a tag:

ActiveTags.Add(card);

UI updates automatically.

3. TrendCardViewModel.cs
Purpose

Represents one trend chart card.

Example:

+-------------------+
| Tank Level        |
|                   |
|      Chart        |
|                   |
+-------------------+

Each card owns:

Tag
Series
RenderableSeries
YVisibleRange
Annotations
Tag
public ScadaTag Tag

Stores:

LT101
Tank Level
0-100%
Series
ObservableCollection<ChartSeriesViewModel>

Stores chart data.

Example:

Actual
Target
Average
Limit
RenderableSeries
ObservableCollection<IRenderableSeries>

Stores visual chart objects.

Example:

FastLineRenderableSeries
FastMountainRenderableSeries

SciChart reads this collection and draws lines.

4. ChartSeriesViewModel.cs
Purpose

Stores actual chart points.

Example:

Actual
Target
Average

Contains:

SeriesName
Offset
DataSeries
DataSeries

Most important property.

XyDataSeries<DateTime,double>

Stores:

Time              Value
-----------------------
10:00:00          50
10:00:01          51
10:00:02          53

Every trend line owns one DataSeries.

Append

Called continuously.

series.Append(
    DateTime.Now,
    value);

Adds new point to graph.

